<title>ITALY: Italy's BCI 1996 net profit stable on 1995. [CORRECTED 22:09 GMT]</title>
<headline>Italy's BCI 1996 net profit stable on 1995. [CORRECTED 22:09 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Parent net profit	 341    vs   342.3</p>
<p>    Net operating profit up 205 or 17.2 pct</p>
<p>(Corrects from &quot;Net operating profit 205 (up 17.2 pct)&quot;</p>
<p>    Ordinary dividend	 165 lire vs 150</p>
<p>    Savings dividend	  195	vs 180</p>
<p>Note - Full company name is Banca Commerciale Italiana (BCI).  </p>
<p>    Net interest income    3,087   vs (up 1.6 pct)</p>
<p>    Total operating income 5,080   vs   4,801.7</p>
<p>    Net operating profit   1,392   vs   1,187</p>
<p>    Total deposits	 121,371   vs (up 13,627)</p>
<p>    Client deposits	 63,490   vs (up  7,166)</p>
<p>    Total loans	    107,340   vs (up 11,129)</p>
<p>    Client loans	    67,294   vs (up  8,900)</p>
<p>    Net equity		 8,196   vs   n/a</p>
<p>Profit before extraordinary</p>
<p>    items and taxes		516   vs   n/a</p>
<p>Note - BCI said dividend payment would be on May 19.</p>
<p>It said the board had approved the outline of a plan to recapitalise BCI France to allow it to reposition itself on the French corporate banking market.</p>
<p>Consolidated results will be examined by the board in March and the shareholders' meeting will be April 24 or 28.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
